<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

<h3>Is MP4 a video or audio format?</h3>
<p>MP4 is a multimedia container format that can store video, audio, subtitles, and other data.</p>

<h3>Is MP4 better than other video formats?</h3>
<p>It depends on your needs. MP4 is widely compatible, but other formats may offer different benefits for editing, storage, or streaming.</p>

<h3>Does 1080p always mean better quality?</h3>
<p>Not necessarily. Resolution is only one factor. Bitrate, codec, and the original video quality also matter.</p>

<hr>
<p><strong>Conclusion:</strong> MP4 is a versatile and widely supported format for everyday videos. Understanding its resolution, codecs, and bitrate can help you choose the right settings for your projects.</p>

